    "typedFields/answers-in-time/long": {
      "what": "sameValue takes about 2 s on a 2,000-character value of nested brackets (`(\\frac{1}{2}+` repeated), growing with roughly the cube of the length (150 ms at 1,000 characters). Met only with --max-length 2000 or more: the pull-request slice stops at 600 and the nightly at 1,000, so that a time finding there means a cost that explodes, not one that depends on the runner.",
      "whyLeft": "No assignment box sends more than 240 characters; a My Math Path box may send 2,000. Bounding it means refusing long input before it is read, which is a verdict change for those inputs.",
      "tracked": "https://github.com/matthewhawkinsus1-crypto/mathmaster-platform/issues/558",
      "repro": {
        "target": "typedFields",
        "source": "known-finding",
        "field": {
          "id": "answer",
          "label": "Answer",
          "inputProfile": "expression",
          "expected": "(x+ 8)^2"
